                                                <h1>Arts and Cultural Production Satellite Account, U.S. and States, 2023
                                                                                        <div class="lead">
            <div class="field field--name-field-lead field--type-string field--label-hidden field--item">New Statistics for 2023; 1998–2022 Updated</div>
      </div>
                            
                        </h1>
                    
                                            <div class="row">
                            <div class="col-md-12 release-body">
                                
            <div class="field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field--item"><p>The Arts and Cultural Production Satellite Account released today by the U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis shows that arts and cultural economic activity, adjusted for inflation, increased 6.6 percent in 2023 after increasing 3.8 percent in 2022 (chart 1 and table 1). By comparison, the broader economy, as measured by real gross domestic product (GDP), increased 2.9 percent in 2023 after increasing 2.5 percent in 2022 (chart 1). Arts and cultural economic activity accounted for 4.2 percent of GDP, or $1.17 trillion, in 2023 (tables 2 and 3).</p><div data-langcode="en" data-entity-type="node" data-entity-uuid="74c0dd63-d591-4745-bce9-3f40f299c22f" data-embed-button="chart_browser" data-entity-embed-display="view_mode:node.embedded" data-entity-embed-display-settings="[]" class="embedded-entity align-center">
